 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "notice",
   "text": "Draft for Jared's approval. Collected word for word from the city-wide rules paragraphs of the neighbourhood guides listed at the bottom (D-202); nothing new was added. Each guide keeps what is specific to it and links here.",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "The rules below apply across Surrey, not just one neighbourhood: zoning and small-scale housing, strata rules, servicing, land rules and taxes, grouped by topic. Each neighbourhood guide keeps what is specific to that area and links back here. Rules change, so confirm anything that matters for a purchase with the City and your lawyer before you remove subjects.",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Property taxes, transfer tax and GST in Surrey",
   "id": "taxes",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Zoning, SSMUH and suites (Surrey): Zoning Bylaw No. 12000 governs (residential zones R1–R6 in the neighbourhood portion; industrial zones in the Highway 99 industrial area; streamside setbacks sit in Part 7A of Zoning 12000 and vary by stream class — no single riparian figure is ever stated). SSMUH (Jul 8, 2024 frame): A maximum of 3 units on lots smaller than 280 m², 4 units on lots larger than 280 m², and up to 6 units on eligible lots of at least 281 m² within 400 m of a frequent bus stop; one secondary suite per house under the BC Building Code; properties not connected to community water and sewer are among the exemptions. Duplexes are the baseline SSMUH form. The Surrey suite rule is its own: A secondary suite is capped at 40% of the principal dwelling's habitable area — never borrowed for another city. The SSMUH changes do not retroactively legalize suites built without permits — verify a suite's permit status before marketing its income. Servicing Bylaw 8830 (1986) applies. Surrey has no Supreme Court registry."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "taxes"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Bare-land strata / strata block: If a lot elsewhere in Surrey is bare-land strata, the BC position is: a bare-land strata lot is strata tenure — Form B diligence (provided within 7 days, max $35 + 25¢/page), depreciation reports on a 5-year cycle for stratas with 5+ lots since July 1, 2024, minimum 10% CRF contribution since November 1, 2023, rental-restriction bylaws void since November 24, 2022, and only 55+ age bylaws valid under SPA ss.123.1/123.2 with May 1, 2023 exemptions; a listing's \"45+\" line is not a valid BC age bylaw."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "taxes"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Rural property taxes (Province) — the regime that actually applies here: as unincorporated Electoral Area A land, taxes are collected under the provincial rural system (Surveyor of Taxes), with Metro Vancouver and school levies on top — no city tax bill exists. Under the Taxation (Rural Area) Act s.11 regime as the Province publishes it: rural property tax notice mailed May 31, deadline to pay July 2, a 5% penalty applied to the unpaid balance on July 3, and an additional 5% penalty on November 1."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "taxes"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Floodplain, farmland and environmental rules in Surrey",
   "id": "flood",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Plan and zoning (Surrey): The in-force check for any Douglas lot is the Surrey 2050 OCP designation (OCP Bylaw 21900, adopted Jun 15, 2026 — never 18020-as-current) plus the lot's zone under Surrey Zoning By-law No. 12000 — not the 1999 Douglas NCP designations that listing text still quotes, which the City states have been superseded. SSMUH position (Surrey, Jul 8, 2024): Duplexes are the baseline small-scale multi-unit form. Coach houses and garden suites in Surrey: Permitted in residential zones that allow detached houses, duplexes and houseplexes; 35 m² minimum and 75 m² maximum, rising to a maximum of 120 m² for lots zoned RA, R2, R2-O and R3 where the principal dwelling has not achieved its maximum floor area. Servicing Bylaw 8830 (1986) applies. Streamside setbacks sit in Part 7A of Zoning 12000 and vary by stream class — no single riparian figure is ever stated."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "flood"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "A secondary suite's habitable floor area may not exceed 40% of the principal dwelling unit — Surrey's own cap, never borrowed — subject on ALR parcels to the ALC rule that a suite sits only inside the principal residence."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "flood"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Secondary suites in Surrey (non-ALR context) are capped at 40% of the principal dwelling's habitable floor area."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "flood"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Streamside / riparian: A lowland parcel's setback is read from its stream's class in Part 7A for that parcel."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "flood"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Riparian / creek rules: Archibald Creek headwaters, Sullivan Heights Creek and Hyland Creek tributaries run through South Newton, and riparian/setback requirements can limit building envelopes on creek-side lots — check City mapping before valuing an addition, a rebuild or an SSMUH scheme on a creek-side parcel."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "flood"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Strata, co-op and age rules in Surrey",
   "id": "strata",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Secondary suites (Surrey frame): one secondary suite may be permitted in a single family, semi-detached or duplex dwelling, its habitable floor area may not exceed 40% of the principal dwelling unit's habitable area under Zoning By-law No. 12000, and it can never be a separate strata lot; the old 90 m² Surrey suite cap is not a current rule — never state it."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "strata"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Short-term rentals (Surrey): a short-term rental is the renting of a dwelling unit by its owner for under 90 consecutive days per patron; only the owner may host, the owner must live at the property as their primary residence, tenants cannot run one, and a business licence at $358 per year is required before operating. A strata short-term rental bylaw is a separate, building-level check."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "strata"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Secondary suites: Surrey-wide, one secondary suite per single family, semi-detached or duplex dwelling unit; a suite is not permitted within a coach house or garden suite; a suite's habitable floor area may not exceed 40% of the principal dwelling unit; a suite is not a separate strata lot."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "strata"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Zoning, suites and small-scale housing in Surrey",
   "id": "zoning",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Short-term rentals (Surrey frame): permitted, owner-only — an owner must host from their principal residence and hold a City business licence at $358/yr (Zoning By-law No. 12000, Part 4 s. B.7(d); Business License By-law No. 13680, s. 60.1), with the City's 2024 corporate report's $350/yr proposal disclosed as a conflict — carry $358 with $350 disclosed, and check the City licence page before quoting either figure."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Fleetwood Plan status: the plan will guide growth over the next 30+ years as SkyTrain extends along Fraser Highway; Stage 1 was endorsed Mar 7, 2022, an updated Stage 1 was endorsed Oct 16, 2023, further changes have been made to align with the Province's Transit Oriented Areas legislation, and Council will consider the updated plan in 2026 — confirm current zoning and plan status with the City before quoting density for a lot."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "OCP / Zoning — Surrey: Surrey Official Community Plan Bylaw 21900 is current — never cite 18020 as current. Surrey Zoning Bylaw 12000 governs. The Crescent Beach Local Area Plan guides Crescent Beach parcels within that frame. White Rock's Zoning Bylaw 2024 No. 2506 and OCP 2017 No. 2220 are White Rock ground only and do not apply to this Surrey ground."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Subdivision + servicing — Surrey Subdivision and Development Bylaw, 1986, No. 8830 (verified on the City's own pages): the bylaw under which subdivision and servicing requirements for a Douglas parcel run; parcel-level requirements are confirmed with the City."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Zoning — Surrey: Surrey Zoning Bylaw, 1993, No. 12000 governs."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "There is no city zoning bylaw to cite: Planning for the non-reserve lands is Metro Vancouver's Electoral Area A Official Community Plan (2018), whose direction is to keep the island agricultural, and there are no new developments of scale."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Zoning: Surrey Zoning Bylaw No. 12000 governs: South Newton lands carry R-series residential zones, with RA at the rural edges toward Colebrook; a parcel's zone and its subdivision minimums are read off the bylaw for that zone."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Zoning: Surrey Zoning By-law No. 12000: — parcel zoning confirmed per parcel in COSMOS."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "zoning"
  },
  {
   "t": "h",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Other things to know about buying in Surrey",
   "id": "other",
   "gen": "cityrules"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Foreclosure / court sales (where met): a settled court process exists (BC Supreme Court Civil Rules 21-7 / 13-5, Practice Direction PD-66, Form 60). Surrey has no Supreme Court registry."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "other"
  },
  {
   "t": "list",
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Heritage frontage: The boulevard follows part of the Semiahmoo Trail, a route in use by 1858, widened for wagons in 1872 and protected by Surrey Heritage Designation Bylaw, 2004, No. 15280."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "other"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Short-term rentals: Surrey permits them only in the operator's own principal residence, owner-only, with a City business licence at $358/year as stated on the City's licence page."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "other"
  },
  {
   "items": [
    [
     {
      "t": "Foreclosure geography: Surrey has no Supreme Court registry."
     }
    ]
   ],
   "t": "list",
   "gen": "cityrules-item",
   "topic": "other"
  },
